1
00:00:58,399 --> 00:01:00,759
He was wearing a thick jacket that day,

2
00:01:01,039 --> 00:01:02,799
sitting there like nothing had happened.

3
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:04,640
Don't even get me started.

4
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:05,799
It was wickedly cold that day.

5
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:06,599
That chilly wind...

6
00:01:06,599 --> 00:01:08,000
cut right through you like a knife.

7
00:01:11,239 --> 00:01:12,280
Then how long...

8
00:01:14,239 --> 00:01:15,200
was he gone?

9
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:19,200
About half an hour, I'd say.

10
00:01:21,599 --> 00:01:22,519
No, no, no.

11
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,599
You're definitely remembering it wrong.

12
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:27,640
He wasn't wearing a jacket then.

13
00:01:28,239 --> 00:01:29,280
What he had on was...

14
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:33,120
an old gray shirt.

15
00:01:35,439 --> 00:01:36,920
It was all wrinkled on him.

16
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,400
During the opera,

17
00:01:39,519 --> 00:01:40,400
he was so cold

18
00:01:40,799 --> 00:01:42,719
he kept burying his head in his collar,

19
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:45,200
shaking like a leaf.

20
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:47,879
I was sitting right behind him.

21
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,640
I remember it clear as day.

22
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:50,799
There's absolutely no doubt about it.

23
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Come off it!

24
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,000
You're just getting senile.

25
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:56,400
The cold wave came early up north this year.

26
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,439
I was bundled up so thick,

27
00:01:57,439 --> 00:01:58,439
and I was still shivering.

28
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,840
How could he just wear a thin shirt?

29
00:02:01,159 --> 00:02:03,000
Nobody acts tough like that.

30
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,120
It was a thin shirt!

31
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:06,920
I'm sure of it!

32
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,120
We were sitting together.

33
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,759
I was right behind him.

34
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:12,360
I even asked him,

35
00:02:12,639 --> 00:02:13,560
"Dressed so light,

36
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:14,639
aren't you freezing?"

37
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:15,919
And he...

38
00:02:16,719 --> 00:02:17,479
didn't even turn his head.

39
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:19,560
Just stiffened his neck and said, "Uncle,

40
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,800
my blood runs hot. I'm burning up."

41
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,840
Yet I saw him shivering all over,

42
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:26,039
pulling out a flat flask,

43
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,879
sneaking gulps of liquor.

44
00:02:29,039 --> 00:02:29,960
That was just him...

45
00:02:30,159 --> 00:02:33,000
freezing, relying on booze, and talking tough.

46
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,159
Right, right.

47
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:36,319
Old Bi,

48
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,919
do you still remember

49
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:43,080
how long he was gone at the time?

50
00:02:44,759 --> 00:02:46,560
It was during the third act.

51
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,639
Halfway through,

52
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,080
right when the chancellor came on stage,

53
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,039
he returned.

54
00:02:51,039 --> 00:02:52,199
Just about half an hour.

55
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,319
Half an hour.

56
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:00,960
So that means...

57
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:05,000
when he first arrived,

58
00:03:05,039 --> 00:03:06,520
he was wearing a jacket.

59
00:03:07,759 --> 00:03:10,199
In between, he left for half an hour.

60
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,000
When he came back,

61
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:13,719
the jacket was gone.

62
00:03:14,039 --> 00:03:14,639
Yeah.

63
00:03:15,879 --> 00:03:16,840
It was so cold.

64
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,439
Why did he insist on sitting there?

65
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,000
It's just his passion.

66
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:23,759
Whenever he's free,

67
00:03:23,759 --> 00:03:25,280
he even loves to sing a few lines.

68
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:28,479
All right.

69
00:03:28,639 --> 00:03:31,120
You folks chat. We'll look around the village, okay?

70
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:31,400
Sure, sure.

71
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:31,800
Sounds good.

72
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:32,520
See you later.

73
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:32,719
Take care.

74
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:33,840
Okay, take care.

75
00:03:34,039 --> 00:03:34,800
Thank you.

76
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,000
Don't mention it. You're welcome.

77
00:03:48,039 --> 00:03:48,599
Come on.

78
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,240
Let's check out the ancestral hall.

79
00:04:33,839 --> 00:04:34,560
Mentor.

80
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,360
You can tell Chen Jun had plenty of time that day.

81
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,680
He was wandering around town the whole time.

82
00:04:44,399 --> 00:04:45,639
Not until the opera ended

83
00:04:45,879 --> 00:04:47,399
did he ride his motorcycle back to the village.

84
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:50,079
By then, it was already past midnight.

85
00:04:53,079 --> 00:04:56,040
Sun Xiaofei's time of death has been confirmed.

86
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,639
It was at 6:00 that evening.

87
00:05:00,879 --> 00:05:05,199
Chen Jun arrived in town at 3:00 that afternoon.

88
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,600
The timeline doesn't match up.

89
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:17,160
You seem quite familiar

90
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,759
with Sun Xiaofei's situation?

91
00:05:20,199 --> 00:05:22,360
Her justifiable defense was once used as a case study.

92
00:05:22,639 --> 00:05:23,800
I looked into it back then.

93
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:28,680
Did Sun Xiaofei's and Chen Jun's families

94
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,319
have any bad blood between them?

95
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:33,199
No.

96
00:05:34,319 --> 00:05:37,000
She went to the Chens' to visit prospective in-laws.

97
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:40,600
Sun Xiaofei and the Ma family

98
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:43,079
got engaged right after junior college graduation.

99
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,639
However, because Sun Xiaofei

100
00:05:45,639 --> 00:05:47,120
was involved in a justifiable defense case

101
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,600
where she killed a thug,

102
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,000
she was traumatized

103
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,959
and spent over a year in a psychiatric hospital.

104
00:05:52,399 --> 00:05:53,279
After she was discharged,

105
00:05:53,319 --> 00:05:54,360
the Mas broke off the engagement,

106
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,120
and she was set to marry into the Chen family.

107
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,759
That day,

108
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:01,000
the Chens kept quiet about what happened,

109
00:06:01,639 --> 00:06:02,560
partly because

110
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,600
Sun Xiaofei had a mental illness.

111
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,720
The killer

112
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:12,879
deliberately chose a time when the Chens were away,

113
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,199
with only their future daughter-in-law there,

114
00:06:17,439 --> 00:06:18,639
to strike out of the blue.

115
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:24,600
What was the name of the guy

116
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,920
who used to harass Sun Xiaofei?

117
00:06:26,399 --> 00:06:27,519
Tong Sheng.

118
00:06:27,519 --> 00:06:27,720
Right.

119
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:28,360
Is he dead?

120
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,600
Died on the spot.

121
00:06:33,759 --> 00:06:35,600
Right now, Chen Jun has plenty of

122
00:06:36,279 --> 00:06:37,519
evidence for his alibi.

123
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:43,000
Do you know anything about Tong Sheng's family?

124
00:06:46,839 --> 00:06:48,439
Tong Sheng's parents, when he was very young,

125
00:06:48,439 --> 00:06:50,920
died of carbon monoxide poisoning.

126
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,800
He was fostered by relatives as a kid.

127
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,839
Later, he couldn't stand it anymore,

128
00:06:55,959 --> 00:06:56,600
ran away,

129
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,639
and drifted into street life.

130
00:06:58,399 --> 00:06:59,959
Sun Xiaofei and he met at a restaurant

131
00:06:59,959 --> 00:07:01,439
while she was working part-time during school.

132
00:07:01,439 --> 00:07:03,120
Tong Sheng was working in the kitchen back then.

133
00:07:05,879 --> 00:07:06,839
As it stands,

134
00:07:10,079 --> 00:07:12,000
only Chen Jun is a suspect.

135
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:16,920
Yet he has a solid alibi.

136
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:22,480
Mentor,

137
00:07:25,199 --> 00:07:26,439
don't you think

138
00:07:26,879 --> 00:07:29,160
his alibi feels a bit...

139
00:07:29,639 --> 00:07:31,120
a bit too deliberate?

140
00:07:33,839 --> 00:07:35,879
What else are you sensing? Speak up.

141
00:07:37,079 --> 00:07:38,879
Could someone have done it for him?

142
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,519
Now you're onto something.

143
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
The cold snap came suddenly this year.

144
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,759
If he stayed outside all day,

145
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,680
wouldn't he freeze to the bone?

146
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,480
Definitely.

147
00:07:53,839 --> 00:07:54,800
So

148
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:01,399
that half hour is the key.

149
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:10,120
Tingting.

150
00:08:10,639 --> 00:08:12,600
Uncle Meng's here for a haircut.

151
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,399
Where's your dad?

152
00:08:15,399 --> 00:08:16,879
Who's this handsome young guy?

153
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,720
This handsome guy is Xiao Chang.

154
00:08:19,759 --> 00:08:21,199
He just transferred to our precinct.

155
00:08:21,279 --> 00:08:22,600
Getting a haircut?

156
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,519
I asked you, where's your dad?

157
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:28,519
My dad's lying inside. He's sick.

158
00:08:28,519 --> 00:08:30,120
Sick? How did he get sick?

159
00:08:30,759 --> 00:08:31,639
Caught a chill.

160
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:33,519
Take me in to see him, quick.

161
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:34,960
Okay.

162
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,399
My dad's right here.

163
00:08:44,799 --> 00:08:45,679
I'll let you talk.

164
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:55,360
Lao Meng.

165
00:08:56,399 --> 00:08:57,279
What brings you here?

166
00:08:57,679 --> 00:08:58,919
I heard you were sick.

167
00:08:58,919 --> 00:08:59,919
Came to check on you.

168
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:01,480
How'd you get sick?

169
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:04,759
Caught a chill watching the opera.

170
00:09:05,399 --> 00:09:06,120
Look at you.

171
00:09:06,919 --> 00:09:07,799
Dressed too light.

172
00:09:08,919 --> 00:09:10,440
Who would've thought?

173
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,320
This cold snap is so brutal this year.

174
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,440
It was never this cold before.

175
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,720
Alright, just rest up and you'll be fine.

176
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,120
Still got some energy.

177
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,000
Let's talk about something else.

178
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,159
Something happened at Chen Changhe's.

179
00:09:26,519 --> 00:09:27,240
Have you heard?

180
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,159
No.

181
00:09:28,679 --> 00:09:29,960
Haven't I been sick?

182
00:09:30,039 --> 00:09:32,279
I've been in bed taking meds.

183
00:09:32,279 --> 00:09:33,759
Haven't stepped out for three days.

184
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,519
What happened to his family?

185
00:09:35,799 --> 00:09:37,960
His prospective daughter-in-law was murdered.

186
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,519
I heard you had a feud with Chen Changhe.

187
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,120
Over homestead land.

188
00:09:44,399 --> 00:09:45,200
Yeah.

189
00:09:45,679 --> 00:09:47,200
That Chen Changhe,

190
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:49,919
he's a real piece of work.

191
00:09:50,759 --> 00:09:53,320
Clearly it was his wall

192
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,679
encroaching on our driveway.

193
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:58,480
Don't know what he told the chief,

194
00:09:58,639 --> 00:09:59,720
but the chief ended up

195
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,360
siding with him.

196
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:02,200
Where am I supposed to get justice?

197
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:04,679
Lao Meng, why don't you judge for yourself?

198
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:07,600
Between his wall and mine,

199
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:09,879
the path used to be 1.7 meters wide.

200
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:12,039
After he built his house,

201
00:10:12,039 --> 00:10:13,919
only 1.5 meters was left.

202
00:10:13,919 --> 00:10:15,399
I can't even get through!

203
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,080
My cart won't fit through.

204
00:10:18,799 --> 00:10:20,200
All I know is, back then,

205
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,799
you made some serious threats.

206
00:10:22,639 --> 00:10:23,399
I did.

207
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:24,600
I said it.

208
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,559
I said I'd kill him.

209
00:10:27,279 --> 00:10:28,240
And he said

210
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,799
he'd kill me too.

211
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,279
We were just fighting.

212
00:10:31,279 --> 00:10:32,919
In the heat of the moment,

213
00:10:32,919 --> 00:10:34,919
you say whatever sounds the nastiest.

214
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,080
Chen Changhe doesn't have your guts.

215
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,120
He's not like you.

216
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,799
You're a man of your word.

217
00:10:45,159 --> 00:10:47,159
What're you getting at, Lao Meng?

218
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:51,399
You don't think it was me...

219
00:10:53,279 --> 00:10:54,399
Come on now.

220
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,240
Lao Meng.

221
00:10:55,919 --> 00:10:59,759
You should know what kind of guy I am.

222
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,279
Besides,

223
00:11:01,879 --> 00:11:03,559
every debt has its debtor.

224
00:11:03,639 --> 00:11:06,039
It's between me and Chen Changhe, right?

225
00:11:06,279 --> 00:11:07,840
No matter what, I wouldn't

226
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,720
take it out on a kid.

227
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,559
On his daughter-in-law, right?

228
00:11:12,879 --> 00:11:14,000
The day you watched the opera,

229
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,159
what were you wearing?

230
00:11:16,919 --> 00:11:18,240
Just a thin jacket.

231
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:19,879
It was freezing.

232
00:11:19,879 --> 00:11:21,279
Why didn't you dress warmer?

233
00:11:25,639 --> 00:11:26,919
That's how I caught a chill.

234
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:28,480
So,

235
00:11:28,639 --> 00:11:30,000
serves me right, doesn't it?

236
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,919
Alright, get some rest. I'm off.

237
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:52,240
Driving to the village and back in half an hour...

238
00:11:52,799 --> 00:11:54,279
That's completely impossible.

239
00:11:55,879 --> 00:11:57,600
Even on a motorcycle,

240
00:11:59,759 --> 00:12:01,480
you'd only make it this far.

241
00:12:13,559 --> 00:12:14,360
Mentor.

242
00:12:14,879 --> 00:12:15,720
Pull over.

243
00:12:16,519 --> 00:12:17,200
What's wrong?

244
00:12:18,039 --> 00:12:19,879
Someone just ran into the woods.

245
00:12:20,399 --> 00:12:21,519
Pull over, pull over!

246
00:12:23,679 --> 00:12:24,639
Where?

247
00:12:25,279 --> 00:12:26,519
It's the middle of the night.

248
00:12:26,519 --> 00:12:27,759
Stop talking nonsense.

249
00:12:28,519 --> 00:12:30,080
Why would anyone run into the woods?

250
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,200
I'll go take a look.

251
00:12:34,399 --> 00:12:34,840
You—

252
00:12:35,639 --> 00:12:36,440
Don't—

253
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:06,879
Xiao Chang!

254
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:09,720
Xiao Chang!

255
00:13:10,559 --> 00:13:11,440
What are you doing?

256
00:13:12,679 --> 00:13:13,440
Come on out.

257
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:14,480
What are you looking for?

258
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:15,200
Mentor.

259
00:13:15,679 --> 00:13:17,159
There really was something just now.

260
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,559
I chased it all the way here.

261
00:13:18,559 --> 00:13:19,279
Where is it?

262
00:13:19,519 --> 00:13:20,600
It's gone now.

263
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:21,960
Stop being paranoid.

264
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,000
Just come on over.

265
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:32,879
It suddenly vanished right here.

266
00:13:36,919 --> 00:13:37,720
Mentor.

267
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,600
Mentor, the soil here is soft.

268
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,120
Wait, Mentor.

269
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:05,879
What?

270
00:14:08,919 --> 00:14:09,600
Mentor!

271
00:14:12,039 --> 00:14:13,039
I dug something up!

272
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,679
A blood-stained jacket.

273
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:29,480
You were right.

274
00:14:30,519 --> 00:14:31,879
There was a third person.

275
00:14:32,879 --> 00:14:34,159
There really was someone else,

276
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:37,720
a third person we didn't see.

277
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:42,759
This jacket is a new style,

278
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:44,639
a name brand, too.

279
00:14:45,679 --> 00:14:47,600
Only a few dozen were sold in town.

280
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:50,480
Judging by this size,

281
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:52,320
the killer has to be

282
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:54,799
between 185 and 190 centimeters tall.

283
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:57,840
What are you sniffing?

284
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,840
Think you're a police dog now?

285
00:15:01,799 --> 00:15:02,519
Mentor,

286
00:15:03,559 --> 00:15:05,039
it smells like cigars.

287
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,000
Smells like Gongzi Brand cigars.

288
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:09,480
Take a sniff.

289
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,320
It is a cigar.

290
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:17,840
Are you sure

291
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:20,399
it's Gongzi Brand?

292
00:15:20,519 --> 00:15:21,320
I'm sure.

293
00:15:21,679 --> 00:15:24,159
A cousin of mine smokes that brand.

294
00:15:24,399 --> 00:15:25,879
Plus, at the crime scene that day,

295
00:15:25,879 --> 00:15:27,240
I smelled it there, too.

296
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:33,919
Right?

297
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:42,759
Slow down.

298
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:53,559
Lao Meng.

299
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:54,879
Hello.

300
00:15:54,919 --> 00:15:55,519
Keeping busy?

301
00:15:55,519 --> 00:15:56,240
Uncle Zhang.

302
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:11,399
We're here.

303
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,000
Hey there.

304
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:20,240
Lao Liu.

305
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:20,840
Lao Meng.

306
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:21,799
How's business?

307
00:16:22,039 --> 00:16:22,840
Not bad.

308
00:16:24,279 --> 00:16:26,720
Got any Gongzi Brand cigarettes?

309
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:27,759
Sure do.

310
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,399
They pack quite a punch, right?

311
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:35,799
You bet.

312
00:16:35,919 --> 00:16:37,679
Most folks can't afford them.

313
00:16:38,559 --> 00:16:39,360
How much?

314
00:16:39,799 --> 00:16:40,679
Three-fifty.

315
00:16:52,679 --> 00:16:53,240
Here you go.

316
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,039
All right, thanks.

317
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:08,920
Who usually buys these cigarettes from you?

318
00:17:13,279 --> 00:17:14,279
You need something?

319
00:17:25,279 --> 00:17:26,119
Thank you.

320
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,319
How did I forget about this guy?

321
00:17:43,559 --> 00:17:44,559
Liu Jianguo.

322
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:48,519
He's been locked up multiple times for fighting,

323
00:17:49,599 --> 00:17:51,119
only got out last year.

324
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,000
Height-wise,

325
00:17:55,559 --> 00:17:57,000
he's almost 1.9 meters tall.

326
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:59,240
If it really comes to blows,

327
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,440
we might be no match for him.

328
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:06,359
Mentor, should we call for backup?

329
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,599
What backup?

330
00:18:09,519 --> 00:18:10,599
That's a waste of police resources.

331
00:18:12,319 --> 00:18:13,759
Know what it means to outsmart someone?

332
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:16,240
Do you?

333
00:18:21,359 --> 00:18:22,240
In a bit,

334
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:23,799
there's something

335
00:18:24,759 --> 00:18:25,680
you need to say.

336
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:27,279
It's very important.
